/09/Day%202%20-%20Major%20Lower%20Body%20Muscles/","source-block-513","Leg day of the Chapter Two resistance training program: quadriceps, hamstrings, glutes, and calves. Each muscle group gets compound movements first, then isolation movements.",["Day 2: Major Lower Body Muscles - YouTube","About"]],["Person/Andrew%20Huberman/Book/26/Protocols/YouTube/26/09/Day%202%20-%20Major%20Lower%20Body%20Muscles/","source-block-692","Sets, reps, and weights are in the book; the video shows form. A work set goes to failure, meaning the point where the movement can no longer be done in good form.",["Day 2: Major Lower Body Muscles - YouTube","About"]],["Person/Andrew%20Huberman/Book/26/Protocols/YouTube/26/09/Day%202%20-%20Major%20Lower%20Body%20Muscles/","source-block-860","Each chapter's transcript comes from the video's captions. Where a caption is plainly wrong, the caption's words are struck through and the correction follows in brackets: peck [pec]. A bracketed word alone fills in a word the captions dropped.",["Day 2: Major Lower Body Muscles - YouTube","About"]],["Person/Andrew%20Huberman/Book/26/Protocols/YouTube/26/09/Day%202%20-%20Major%20Lower%20Body%20Muscles/","source-block-1113","Video",["Day 2: Major Lower Body Muscles - YouTube"]],["Person/Andrew%20Huberman/Book/26/Protocols/YouTube/26/09/Day%202%20-%20Major%20Lower%20Body%20Muscles/","block-1cf1b3c9-2029-44d6-8b84-d7073d465886","00:00 Leg day overview",["Day 2: Major Lower Body Muscles - YouTube","Video"]],["Person/Andrew%20Huberman/Book/26/Protocols/YouTube/26/09/Day%202%20-%20Major%20Lower%20Body%20Muscles/","source-block-1306","Transcript",["Day 2: Major Lower Body Muscles - YouTube","Video","00:00 Leg day overview"]],["Person/Andrew%20Huberman/Book/26/Protocols/YouTube/26/09/Day%202%20-%20Major%20Lower%20Body%20Muscles/","source-block-1346","Person/Andrew Huberman",["Video","00:00 Leg day overview","Transcript"]],["Person/Andrew%20Huberman/Book/26/Protocols/YouTube/26/09/Day%202%20-%20Major%20Lower%20Body%20Muscles/","source-block-1380","00:00 In chapter 2 on exercise, I refer to the foundational fitness program and day two being the day that you directly target your legs, meaning your quadricep muscles, your hamstrings, your glutes, and your calves.",["00:00 Leg day overview","Transcript","Person/Andrew Huberman"]],["Person/Andrew%20Huberman/Book/26/Protocols/YouTube/26/09/Day%202%20-%20Major%20Lower%20Body%20Muscles/","source-block-1623","00:11 So first I'm going to demonstrate compound exercises to target your quadriceps. So we're going to start with a back squat, then we'll do a front squat. And then a couple other squat variations.",["00:00 Leg day overview","Transcript","Person/Andrew Huberman"]],["Person/Andrew%20Huberman/Book/26/Protocols/YouTube/26/09/Day%202%20-%20Major%20Lower%20Body%20Muscles/","source-block-1933","00:21 These are designed to be movements that you can generally find the equipment to [for] in any gym. Or you could put together in a home gym.",["00:00 Leg day overview","Transcript","Person/Andrew Huberman"]],["Person/Andrew%20Huberman/Book/26/Protocols/YouTube/26/09/Day%202%20-%20Major%20Lower%20Body%20Muscles/","block-901e5f09-94a2-4fee-bf5f-8109c25fb004","00:27 Exercise/Body/Strength/Back Squat",["Day 2: Major Lower Body Muscles - YouTube","Video"]]],"format_version":5}